# Vercel Environment Variables Reference
# ======================================
# Copy these exact variable names when setting up in Vercel Dashboard
# Go to: Project Settings → Environment Variables → Add New

# Supabase Configuration
# Get these values from: https://app.supabase.com → Your Project → Settings → API

# Example values (replace with your actual credentials):
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=zgcfzhifbjwwfgtggazb
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://zgcfzhifbjwwfgtggazb.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6InpnY2Z6aGlmYmp3d2ZndGdnYXpiIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NjkyNDgzNDAsImV4cCI6MjA4NDgyNDM0MH0.pmTSwPFdMrZJuXahk57mhWipB6BrXpcnE4498uOsStY

# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# ----------------
# 1. Variable names are CASE-SENSITIVE and must start with VITE_
# 2. In Vercel, select ALL environments: Production, Preview, Development
# 3. After adding variables, you MUST manually redeploy (variables don't auto-deploy)
# 4. For fresh build, uncheck "Use existing Build Cache" when redeploying
